nding rates. If these market conditions pe","full_chars":1200},"source":{"provider":"tinyfish","endpoint":"search+fetch","upstream":"https://www.boj.or.jp/en/mopo/mpmdeci/state_2022/k221220a.htm","retrieved_at":"2026-09-04T15:57:01.607Z","cached":true,"citation":"https://www.boj.or.jp/en/mopo/mpmdeci/state_2022/k221220a.htm"},"relevance":0.4359},{"id":"d-CL-0016-0","lane":"doc","world":"live","driver":{"client_id":"CL-0016","key":"currency:JPY","dimension":"currency","value":"JPY","weight_pct":43.59},"status":"candidate","tier":"structural","query":"JPY carry trade and intervention history","doc":{"title":"Concluding Panel Discussion: Growth, Integration, and Monetary Policy in East Asia","url":"https://www.imes.boj.or.jp/research/papers/english/me25-s1-10.pdf","final_url":"https://23.212.62.200/research/papers/english/me25-s1-10.pdf","excerpt":"233\nConcluding Panel Discussion: \nGrowth, Integration, and \nMonetary Policy in East Asia\nIntroductory Remarks\nAkinari Horii\nBank of Japan\nNow it is time for the concluding panel, where we are going to discuss growth, \nintegration, and monetary policy in East Asia from policy perspectives.\nWe have discussed already a number of issues, policy issues, in the previous session.\nTherefore, this discussion is quite a natural extension from that one. But there are a\nfew specific questions I would like to raise here, most of which were covered in the\nprevious session. Let me start with the one not covered.\nThe first question concerns East Asian economic and financial integration with \nthe rest of the world. Because of this integration, the degree of competition in \nproduct markets increased in the global marketplace. As a result, the pricing power of\nproducers in national markets has weakened.\nAl","full_chars":1200},"source":{"provider":"tinyfish","endpoint":"search+fetch","upstream":"https://23.212.62.200/research/papers/english/me25-s1-10.pdf","retrieved_at":"2026-09-04T15:57:01.607Z","cached":true,"citation":"http